<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lobamba</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lobamba is the traditional, royal and legislative capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eswatini">Eswatini</a>, in the Ezulwini valley between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mbabane">Mbabane</a> and Manzini. It is the seat of the queen mother and the Parliament, and the site of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/incwala">Incwala</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umhlanga">Umhlanga</a> ceremonies, the national museum and the memorial of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sobhuza-ii">Sobhuza II</a>. Mbabane is the administrative capital.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lobamba.jpg" alt="Lobamba" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bernard Gagnon · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Parliament_building_of_Eswatini,_Lobamba.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
